      "id": "agents-commands",
      "name": "Custom agents and commands",
      "who": "the developer using OpenCode",
      "main": true,
      "reach": 0,
      "evidence": "Markdown or JSON files in .opencode or the global config (packages/opencode/src/config/agent.ts, command.ts); `opencode agent create` drafts an agent with the model (cli/cmd/agent.ts). No supported undo: the files are versioned only by the user's own git (GOV-05 1), and the generator writes outside any session, so session revert does not cover it. Reach 0 because the path has no undo; the AI draft would otherwise read as reach 2, which DEL-04 1 would not support.",
      "confidence": "high",
      "reach_name": "Engineers only"
    },
    {
      "id": "project-instructions",
      "name": "Standing instructions for a project (AGENTS.md)",
      "who": "the developer using OpenCode",
      "main": true,
      "reach": 1,
      "evidence": "The built-in /init command has the agent create or update AGENTS.md (packages/opencode/src/command/template/initialize.txt), and people edit it in chat. Edits made in a session are snapshotted and the session can be reverted from the TUI or API (packages/opencode/src/session/revert.ts, snapshot/). Reach 1, not 2: the agent drafts the file, but DEL-04 is 1, so the criteria do not support reach 2.",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "reach_name": "Self-serve"
    },
    {
      "id": "models-providers",
      "name": "Which models and providers it uses",
      "who": "the developer using OpenCode",
      "main": true,
      "reach": 1,
      "evidence": "Providers are added and removed with `opencode auth login` and `opencode providers logout` (packages/opencode/src/cli/cmd/providers.ts:492-501), and the model is chosen in the model picker, which keeps recent choices (packages/opencode/src/provider/provider.ts:2035). Undo is selecting the previous model or logging out. Defaults set by editing opencode.json have no product history. Undo rule used in this field test: a kind has undo when the product keeps the earlier version, or when the change is a selection, toggle or add-and-remove that the same supported path reverses exactly; free-text or multi-field edits with no kept version have none.",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "reach_name": "Self-serve"
